4. Keep `SEQUENCE_LENGTH = 60`.
5. Keep `DIRECTION_THRESHOLD = 0.0015` unchanged.
6. Do NOT change the existing multi-step validation behavior for options data.
7. Do NOT use the custom statistical confidence score for BUY/SELL/HOLD decisions. Keep the model's direction softmax confidence as the trading confidence.
8. Add a simple class-distribution check for SELL/HOLD/BUY. Do not add class weighting unless the existing class distribution clearly requires it.
9. Do not change the FTP/data-loading logic except fix the hardcoded FTP credentials if necessary by reading them from environment variables.
10. Fix the local Windows data path so it uses a safe raw string or forward slashes.

Most importantly: preserve the current model architecture and behavior. I only want these targeted fixes, not a complete rewrite.
